Before Starting...*** Print this document so that it may be referred to while using BoardEditor. ***Setup:1.  Place the folder StepDesigner in the folder entitled Step On It! Folder.2.  Inside Step On It! Folder is a file entitled SOI Boards.  Single-click SOI Boards and select Duplicate from the File menu.  Name the copy SOI Boards-Edit.  (This file will be used to edit the original levels.)3.  Open StepDesigner  and launch BoardEditor  by double-clicking on the program icon.4.  Select Open from the File menu.5.  Locate the file entitled MyBoardSet and select Open.  To edit the original levels, locate SOI Boards-Edit (which is in Step On It! Folder ) and select Open.6.  Double-click on Board 1 (or the level to be edited).Editing:To use BoardEditor, single-click on an object and place it on the board.  To change the properties of an object, single-click the appropriate box or boxes and then place it on the board.  See below for definitions of the various properties.Starting Bonus - amount of time Ted has to complete a level.Block Properties- Supportive:  Ted can stand on the block and remove it.- Permanent:  Ted cannot stand on the block, but can remove it.- Supportive & Permanent:  Ted can stand on the block, but cannot remove it.- Neither:  Ted cannot stand on the block and cannot remove it - Background.Badguy Properties- Start Delay:  amount of time before the first badguy emerges (spawns) from the spawn block (i.e. Wheelie’s starting point).- Spawn Delay:  amount of time between spawns (Note: It affects the lifespan of the badguy).Starting Direction- left/up:  the initial direction of a badguy- right/down:  the initial direction of a badguy- Alternate:  changes the direction of badguys that emerge from a spawn block (i.e. Wheelie)- Seek Player:  currently not availableSet Starting Direction- Player 1:  single-click to place Ted (blue) on the board- Player 2:  single-click to place Ted (green) on the boardChallenge Board- Percent UltraBuster:  determines what percent of the Gargoyle’s projectiles are UltraBusters (Green or Red/Blue weapons that destroy Ted’s blocks)- Percent Badguy:  determines what percent of the Gargoyle’s projectiles are Badguys- thrown badguy:  determines which badguy the Gargoyle will throwSaving & Playing:1.  At this time, the only way to save an edited board is to close the window and select Save Changes.2.  To play the level, select Quit from the File menu.  Double-click on Step On It!  located in  Step On It! Folder .3.  Select Load Board Set from the File menu.  Double-click on StepDesigner.  Double-click on MyBoardSet.4.  Select Set Starting Board from the File menu.  Enter the level and single-click on OK.